course: dictionary
lesson: 553
title: Attract: pull and draw near
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word attract has more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. To attract means to pull something towards itself, or to make people or animals want to come near.
explain: «Magnets attract iron.» Here attract means pull. «Bright flowers attract bees.» Here it means make come near. Ask yourself what word would fit, then try it in the sentence: "pull" or "draw near" should both make sense.
explain: Some phrases use attract in a special way. «Opposites attract» is a saying, and «attract attention» means make people notice you. Attract crowds means bring lots of people together.
fact: To attract means to pull something towards itself, or to draw someone or something near.
fact: «Opposite poles of two magnets attract and like poles repel.»
fact: Magnets attract things made of iron, nickel and steel.
fact: «Bright flowers attract bees»: the colour and smell draw insects in.
fact: The noun is attraction, and the adjective is attractive, as in «an attractive garden».
exercise: «Magnets attract iron.» What does attract mean here? | Make it hot | *Pull towards itself | Push away | Hide from view
exercise: «Leftover bread attracts rats.» What does attracts mean? | *Makes rats want to come near | Makes rats fall asleep | Makes rats grow bigger | Makes rats go away
exercise: Which word is the noun form of attract? | attracting | *attraction | attracted | attractive
test: Which poles of magnets attract each other? | Two north poles | *A north pole and a south pole | None of them | Two south poles
test: Which force attracts objects towards each other, which is why we fall down? | *Gravity | Sound | Light | Friction
exam: Which sentence uses attract to mean make come near? | *«Lotus flowers can warm themselves to attract insects.» | «Ducks like peas and oats.» | «Spiders can make up to seven kinds of silk.» | «Lightning strikes tall trees.»
